Fully turn off PC:
1.	Open Choose a power plan
2.	Open Choose what the power buttons do
3.	Click Change settings that are currently unavailable
4.	Deactivate Turn on fast startup & press save

Power plan to Ultimate Performance:
1. Open Command Prompt on Administrator
2. Paste powercfg -duplicatescheme e9a42b02-d5df-448d-aa00-03f14749eb61
3. Run that command
4. Open Choose a power plan
5. Select Ultimate Performance

Boost FPS in a game/app:
1.	Launch the application
2.	Open Task Manager
3.	Right click on the application
4.	Select Go to details
5.	Right click again on the preferred application
6.	Select Set priority and then high (NOT Realtime)

Boost FPS:
1.	Press win + R
2.	Type SystemPropertiesPerformance
3.	Select Adjust for best performance
4.	Click apply
5.	Restart PC

Fix memory issues:
1.	Press win + R
2.	Type MDSCHED.exe
3.	Select Restart now and check for problems

Disable startup apps:
1.	Open Task Manager
2.	Select Startup apps
3.	Deactivate the non important ones

Issues, but not sure:
1.	Open Event Viewer
2.	Select what needed and look through
1.	Red symbols: bad
2.	Yellow symbols: if repetitive, bad

Fix system errors:
1.	Enter CMD on Administrator
2.	Type Get-MMAgent
If “MemoryCompression: True” & system more than 7gb
-	Type Disable-MMAgent -mc
If “MemoryCompression: False” & system less than 8gb
-	Type Enable-MMAgent -mc
3.	Restart device

Fix processors:
1. Search "msconfig"
2. Go to "Boot"
3. At Advanced Options, click on Number of processors and choose the highest amount
4. Restart device

Make Windows faster (no animations):
1. Search "Advanced System Settings"
2. Press "Settings" at "Performance"
3. Choose "Adjust for best performance

Deactivate background services:
1. Windows key + R
2. Type msconfig
3. Click services
4. Press "Hide all Microsoft Services"
5. Disable what not needed

Deactivating useless services:
1. Open Services
2. Right click on the process, you don't need
3. Select Properties and and choose for startup Manual
4. Click apply

In generall some advices:
1. deactivate as many useless settings as possible
2. Deactivate background apps
3. Update Windows
4. Activate Game Mode
5. Activate Storage Sense

Fix hardware issues:
1. Windows key + R
2. Type MSDT.exe -ID DEVICEDIAGNOSTIC
3. Click enter
4. Click on advanced and select Apply repairs automatically
5. Click next
6. After it scanned, press apply fix
7. Restart PC

